{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>YHWH</b> — Because many found [written] 'Elohim of hosts,' they said that [here] He placed a sign in His host. And according to the plain sense, which is the way of brevity, like 'and the prophecy of Oded the prophet' (2 Chronicles 15:8), which is [to be understood as] 'and the prophecy — the prophecy of Oded the prophet'; so too this: 'YHWH, Elohim, Elohim of hosts,' who are the host of heaven." "<b>And the meaning of עשנת</b> — a stative verb, like 'and Mount Sinai smoked entirely' (Exodus 19:18). As though smoke rose up to You at the time of Your people's prayer, and behold the prayer was like smoke, in the manner of 'smoke went up in His anger' (Psalms 74:1)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 80, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:32.030813513Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}